  - computational marketing
abstract: >-
  Computational companion to Brand Coherence Field Theory (BCFT). BCFT models
  brand meaning as a family of probability distributions over a semantic space
  and defines coherence as (negative) divergence from an ideal brand
  distribution on a statistical manifold. This repository provides the formal
  apparatus and executed experiments: real divergences (Kullback-Leibler,
  Jensen-Shannon), Fisher-Rao geodesics, and natural-gradient coherence flows
  on the probability simplex, together with a fully reproducible Python
  pipeline, a synthetic dataset, and the compiled technical report.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ricabreu/bcft-simulation'
